detailed_description:
[Shot 1] Begin @motion at source frame 0 and follow its opening movement phrase without copying its visible content. Begin in the same first-person paratrooper viewpoint and Classic Doom 1993 visual language as @style_base. The camera descends beneath a canvas parachute over a war-torn Dutch village at dawn. Other Allied parachutes drift at different depths, anti-aircraft bursts expand into coarse pixel smoke, and fields, canals, tiled roofs, and a church tower grow steadily larger below. Keep all movement physically continuous and preserve the reference's low-resolution texture rhythm rather than smoothing it into modern realism.

The viewpoint swings gently toward a damaged stone farmhouse. Boots strike the muddy ground, the parachute canopy collapses behind the camera, and the same first-person momentum becomes a short sprint between hedgerows. A period weapon rises naturally into the lower frame. The camera reaches a splintered doorway and pushes inside without a cut. End while exterior dawn light remains visible behind and a dark timber corridor is emerging ahead; preserve the forward motion through the boundary.

overall_soundscape:
Wind rush and canvas flutter during descent give way to a heavy landing, muddy footfalls, distant artillery, scattered rifle fire, wood creaks, and a close doorframe scrape. Keep the sound spatial and game-world diegetic.

non_diegetic_music:
@motion_audio supplies only weak rhythmic timing for the newly generated score; do not directly reuse its waveform. Low martial drums and a restrained ominous brass pulse build gradually beneath the descent, remaining secondary to the battlefield ambience.

